      { term: 'Positioning Map', definition: 'A strategic visual tool plotting competitors on two key dimensions to reveal market gaps, opportunities, and your ideal competitive position.', example: 'A positioning map of streaming services on price vs. content volume reveals a gap: no service offers premium original content at a budget price, exactly where a new entrant could compete.', sentence: 'The positioning map clearly shows a gap in the market: no one is offering enterprise-grade security at SMB-friendly prices.' }
