      { takeaway: 'Dilution compounds, but the pie should grow faster', detail: 'Selling 20% three times leaves you with 51.2%, not 40%. But if each round 10x\'s the company value, 51.2% of $1B is far better than 100% of $1M. Optimize for pie size, not slice size.' },
      { takeaway: 'Terms matter more than valuation', detail: 'A $50M valuation with 2x participating liquidation preferences can be worse than a $30M valuation with standard 1x non-participating terms. Read every line of the term sheet, the devil is in the details.' }
