            { label: 'Pause growth spending and invest in support infrastructure: AI chatbot for common issues, knowledge base, in-app help, and hire 5 support agents, then resume scaling once response time is back under 4 hours', consequence: 'Excellent operational scaling discipline. You can\'t scale customers without scaling support systems. The AI chatbot and knowledge base can handle 60-70% of queries at near-zero marginal cost, keeping unit economics healthy. Pausing growth temporarily to fix the foundation is always better than scaling on a cracking foundation.', score: 3 },
            { label: 'Outsource all support to a cheap third-party call center', consequence: 'Cheap outsourced support often worsens quality further. For a SaaS product, support agents need deep product knowledge. Generic call center reps giving wrong answers will increase ticket volume, not reduce it. Quality support is a scaling investment, not a cost to minimize.', score: 1 }
