      'Correct! The AOL-Time Warner merger is the textbook case of culture clash destroying an M&A deal. Internet-era "cowboys" and traditional media executives had fundamentally different values, work styles, and priorities. Integration was so toxic that employees refused to collaborate. McKinsey\'s research shows culture clash is the #1 reason 70% of mergers fail.',
      'While the dot-com bust didn\'t help, the primary failure was cultural incompatibility and integration breakdown. AOL\'s fast-moving startup culture clashed with Time Warner\'s traditional corporate hierarchy. The lesson: culture eats M&A strategy for breakfast.'
