      'Allocating 70/30 to digital vs. legacy, creating an autonomous digital unit, accelerating self-cannibalization like Apple did, and rejecting the acquisition at the S-curve inflection point, scoring 12/12.',
      'Innovation strategy requires the courage to disrupt yourself before someone else does. Every great transformation, Apple (iPod → iPhone), Netflix (DVD → streaming), Amazon (retail → AWS), required sacrificing short-term profits for long-term dominance. The companies that fail (Kodak, Nokia, Blockberry) all saw the disruption coming and chose to protect the present instead of building the future.'
