        recap: 'The line at the bottom is the whole lesson: Chandler wrote it in 1962 and Nadella proved it in 2014. Windows, Office and Xbox were not lazy, they were arranged to compete with each other, so cloud work could not happen until the arrangement changed, and $300B became $3T. Lesson 6 showed scaling breaking companies that added headcount without changing how that headcount was organized. Pick the structure your strategy needs, then pay the cost that structure comes with.',
