      'The $429 bread maker served as a price anchor. Before its introduction, customers compared $279 to "not buying", expensive vs. free. With the anchor, the comparison became $279 vs. $429, a bargain vs. expensive. The anchor changed the reference frame from "is this worth $279?" to "I\'m saving $150!" Same product, same price, 2x the sales.'
